ommon words\n    82→\n    83→### LOW\n    84→5. **Mention count doesn't include aliases**\n    85→   - Problem: \"the Prince Prospero\" shows 3 mentions, but \"Prospero\" appears 18 times\n    86→   - The combined count should be ~21\n    87→   - Location: Mention counting logic\n    88→\n    89→## Recommended Next Fix (Attempt 21)\n    90→\n    91→### Priority: Populate Structured Profile Fields (quickest path to 8.0)\n    92→\n    93→The profile generation is now running and producing good content in `descriptions`. The issue is that `appearance`, `personality`, and `voice_guidance` remain null.\n    94→\n    95→**Investigation needed:**\n    96→1. Check how `_generate_character_profile()` handles the LLM response\n    97→2. The LLM may be returning unstructured text that goes to `descriptions`\n    98→3. Need to either:\n    99→   a. Modify LLM prompt to return structured JSON with appearance/personality/voice_guidance\n   100→   b. Post-process the descriptions text to extract structured fields\n   101→   c. Modify the code that populates Character model to also set structured fields\n   102→\n   103→**Expected Impact:** +0.15+ points on Profiles (6→7), reaching 8.0 threshold\n   104→\n   105→## What NOT to Try Again\n   106→- Pre-merge substring matching (attempts 17-18) - FAILED\n   107→- Prompt-based rules (attempts 3, 14) - ineffective alone\n   108→- Context window adjustments (attempts 7-15) - insufficient\n   109→\n   110→## Fix History\n   111→\n   112→### Attempts 1-18\n   113→See git history and previous EVALUATION_STATE.md entries.\n   114→\n   115→### Attempt 19 - SUCCESS ✓\n   116→- **Change:** POST-PROCESSING cross-character alias fix\n   117→- **Files Modified:** `src/agents/characters.py` (added `_fix_misplaced_aliases()` method)\n   118→- **Result:** SUCCESS - Prospero alias correctly moved to Prince Prospero\n   119→- **Score Impact:** +1.0 overall (6.70 → 7.70)\n   120→- **Status:** Fix is working\n   121→\n   122→### Attempt 20 - PARTIAL SUCCESS\n   123→- **Change:** Adaptive MIN_MENTIONS_FOR_PROFILE threshold for short texts\n   124→- **Files Modified:** `src/analyzer.py` lines 1013-1025\n   125→- **Result:** PARTIAL - Profile stage runs (26.65s, 3 LLM calls, 2 items)\n   126→- **BUT:** Structured fields (appearance/personality/voice_guidance) still null\n   127→- **Score Impact:** +0.15 overall (7.70 → 7.85)\n   128→- **Status:** Profile generation works, but output format needs adjustment\n   129→\n   130→### Attempt 21 - ANALYSIS COMPLETE\n   131→- **Change:** Populate structured profile fields (appearance, personality, voice_guidance)\n   132→- **Files Modified:** `src/analyzer.py` lines 1630-1806\n   133→- **Root Cause:** `_generate_character_profile()` was returning profile text which was stored in legacy `descriptions` field, but never populating the structured fields added in F8\n   134→- **Fix Details:**\n   135→  1. Modified LLM prompt to request structured JSON with appearance/personality/voice_guidance fields\n   136→  2. Updated return signature to include structured fields (now returns 6-tuple instead of 3-tuple)\n   137→  3. Updated calling code (line 1113) to unpack and store structured fields on character object\n   138→  4. Added fallback: if LLM doesn't return structured fields, use secondary LLM call to structure the profile text\n   139→- **Smoke Test:** Code runs without errors, all 444 unit tests pass\n   140→- **Pipeline Run:** Completed in 8m 37s\n   141→  - Character Profiles: 39.4s, 5 LLM calls, 2 items, 2 high confidence\n   142→  - Total: 28 LLM calls, 43,037 tokens\n   143→- **Status:** Ready for evaluation\n   144→\n   145→## Next Action\n   146→**Phase:** awaiting_evaluation\n   147→Evaluate the analysis output to verify structured profile fields are now populated correctly.\n   148→\n   149→Expected score improvement: 6/10 → 7/10 on Character Profiles (+0.15 overall → 8.0 total)\n   150→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it woul