{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QQyxKnK8Uzahx52qEz4roJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"metadata\": {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n     4→    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n     5→    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n     6→    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n     7→    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n     8→    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n     9→    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    10→    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n    11→  },\n    12→  \"structure\": [\n    13→    {\n    14→      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n    15→      \"title\": null,\n    16→      \"index\": 1,\n    17→      \"start_position\": 28,\n    18→      \"end_position\": 13811,\n    19→      \"word_count\": 2443,\n    20→      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    21→      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    22→      \"children\": [],\n    23→      \"characters_present\": [\n    24→        \"Prince Prospero\",\n    25→        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n    26→        \"Courtiers\",\n    27→        \"Musicians\",\n    28→        \"Buffoons\",\n    29→        \"Improvisatori\",\n    30→        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n    31→        \"Beauty\"\n    32→      ],\n    33→      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by sharp pains, profuse bleeding, and scarlet stains that isolate victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, castellated abbey, sealing all entrances with iron gates and furnaces to ensure total isolation. Inside, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored chambers, each lit by blood-red firelight streaming through stained-glass windows, culminating in a black room with scarlet panes where a massive ebony clock chimes hourly, halting the revelry and instilling dread. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death—cloaked in grave-habits and drenched in blood—enters unchallenged, moving slowly through the chambers until confronting Prince Prospero, who, enraged, pursues him with a dagger but collapses dead upon reaching the black room; the figure is revealed to be the plague itself, and one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"Prospero\"\n    42→      ],\n    43→      \"role\": null,\n    44→      \"appearance\": null,\n    45→      \"personality\": null,\n    46→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    47→      \"descriptions\": [\n    48→        {\n    49→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a defiant and arrogant noble who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the plague, ultimately meeting his demise after pursuing a mysterious figure believed to be the Red Death. His actions reflect a pattern of harmful disregard for others' lives, culminating in his own death and the mass fatalities of his guests.\",\n    50→          \"source_position\": 11148,\n    51→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    52→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    53→        }\n    54→      ],\n    55→      \"relationships\": {},\n    56→      \"evidence\": [\n    57→        {\n    58→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero is enraged by the presence of the Red Death figure and demands immediate execution\",\n    59→          \"quote\": \"insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n    60→          \"position\": 11148,\n    61→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    62→        },\n    63→        {\n    64→          \"sta