 Death—cloaked in grave-habits and drenched in blood—enters unchallenged, moving slowly through the chambers until confronting Prince Prospero, who, enraged, pursues him with a dagger but collapses dead upon reaching the black room; the figure is revealed to be the plague itself, and one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a defiant and arrogant noble who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the plague, ultimately meeting his demise after pursuing a mysterious figure believed to be the Red Death. His actions reflect a pattern of harmful disregard for others' lives, culminating in his own death and the mass fatalities of his guests.\",\n          \"source_position\": 11148,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero is enraged by the presence of the Red Death figure and demands immediate execution\",\n          \"quote\": \"insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero is consumed by rage and shame, leading him to pursue the figure despite fear\",\n          \"quote\": \"maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers\",\n          \"position\": 12389,\n