in to erode their sense of security. At midnight, a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, draped in funeral shrouds and stained with blood, moving with unnatural calm through the chambers. No one dares stop him, and his presence grows more menacing with each step. Prince Prospero, consumed by rage and disbelief, confronts the figure with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon reaching the black room. In that moment, the truth is revealed: the figure is not a guest, but the plague incarnate, having infiltrated the abbey through the very isolation it was meant to prevent. The clock stops, darkness descends, and one by one, every reveler succumbs to the Red Death, their lives extinguished in the same manner as those outside.\\n\\nThe narrative concludes with the complete annihilation of the revelers, underscoring the futility of attempting to escape mortality through wealth, power, or denial. Prince Prospero’s arrogance in believing he could outwit death by sequestering himself and indulging in pleasure is his ultimate downfall. His relationship with his courtiers—built on privilege and spectacle—collapses under the weight of shared fate. The turning point comes not with a battle or revelation, but with the silent, inevitable arrival of the Red Death, which penetrates even the most fortified sanctuary. The story ends not with triumph, but with the grim realization that death is universal, indifferent, and inescapable, rendering all earthly defenses meaningless.\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"identity\",\n        \"ambition\",\n        \"loss\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"model\": 